# Copy to .env.local and fill in what you use.

# --- AI features ---
# Required for: prescription extraction, weekly analysis, check-in drafts, doc chat.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Claude model override (default: claude-opus-4-8)
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-opus-4-8

# Required for document chat (RAG embeddings, voyage-4).
VOYAGE_API_KEY=
# VOYAGE_MODEL=voyage-4

# --- Database ---
# Leave unset to use the embedded PGlite database at .data/pglite (zero config).
# Point at a real Postgres (with the pgvector extension available) to use it instead.
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://user:pass@localhost:5432/showprep
#
# Three-branch model (Neon project "neon-amber-park", aged-resonance-61061629), see VIK-83:
#   production - the real Neon default/"main" branch. Only Vercel's Production
#     environment ever points here. Never point .env.local at it.
#   test       - a personal scratch mirror of production, for Vik's own local
#     debugging against real Postgres instead of PGlite. Point .env.local's
#     DATABASE_URL here (`neonctl cs test`) when you need real Postgres.
#     Reset anytime with `pnpm db:reset-test` (re-syncs to production's
#     current state).
#   staging    - a demo branch for anything shown to Mike/John/Jake or anyone
#     outside the project. Deliberately never contains real personal health
#     data - it's populated only via migrate + `pnpm seed`, never via a
#     parent-reset from production. Reset anytime with `pnpm db:reset-staging`.

# --- Security ---
# Bearer token the mobile companion must send to /api/ingest/*.
# Leave unset to allow unauthenticated ingest in local dev.
INGEST_API_KEY=

# Secret used to sign per-account session cookies (see lib/auth.ts). Leave
# unset to disable the login gate entirely (local dev default). Generate one
# with: openssl rand -base64 32
SESSION_SECRET=

# --- Portfolio demo (optional) ---
# When set, the login page shows a "Portfolio demo" card with a one-click
# "Enter demo" button. Set it EQUAL to a specific account's passcode (see
# scripts/backfill-accounts.ts) so the button logs in as that account.
# Leave unset for a private (non-demo) deployment.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_DEMO_PASSWORD=
